Z||000000||Philphine||10-07-2001||11:12 AM||||just playing with ideas for the next stereo projects. i'm kind of in that mode right now (it's also why i can't get one car done and decent).  <P>you know how the carpets kind of molded to to the floor shape? if i made some speaker pods and tried to put them under the carpet, could i take a heat gun or something and reshape it? nothing to tricky, in fact i'd just be trying to flatten it out a bit around the dead pedal area. <P>also, i don't want 4x10s but in my indy if i change speakers i want to try to keep them in the same spot. since i'll need to make a plate, do you think i'd get anything out of trying to aim the speaker (not just the tweeter) while i'm at it? maybe toward the center of the windshield to help staging some? i'd want this to be an intentionally simple system so no processor plans for later (beyond what might be included in a head unit). <P>open to any and all weird ideas.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||10-07-2001||06:27 PM||||That stock carpet is pretty stout.  I seriously doubt you could remold it.<P>Try some 5 1/4" components in the dash.  They will fit, but they won't lie flat against the inside lip.  You'll need spacers.  I don't see why you'd need to aim them.  I had them in the Grape Ape and they worked just fine.||||reg||1
